Z||000000||DjKid||10-01-2000||04:11 AM||||I need a good idea of where to find a Turbo... for a good price, prolly next summer, for a 3.1(3.2)l Chevy v6... I'm wanting to go turbo.. but I might break down and go Nitrous.. any ideas? Pros? Cons?<P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe - <A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Greg Piet||10-01-2000||06:54 AM||||There are oodles of threads about this, but here is the short story of my take...<BR>Speed isnt cheap!<BR>You can get a GOOD tubo kit from <A HREF="http://www.designonesystems.com" TARGET=_blank>www.designonesystems.com</A> <BR>but if you do not NEED  air conditioning<BR>i would go with a supercharger for a little less ( I think ) at <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/fiero_catalog.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/fiero_catalog.htm</A> <P>I will not discuss NOS because I personally dont like it, but others love it!<P>I am guessing the 3.1 is the same block as the 2.8, just bored and stroked with the fancy crankshaft, etc...<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 10-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||10-01-2000||07:05 AM||||BEWARE!!!!!!!<BR>looking at RSM's site<BR>the file <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/supercharger.doc" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/supercharger.doc</A> <P>is infected!<BR>My Norton anti virus 2000   told me it had <BR>"w97M.class" virus!!!!!<BR>||||reg||1
